claim.claim-text:
receiving from the serving access node, with a control channel message, a set of beams to measure comprising an identification of each beam to measure and determined time periods to perform the measurement;
measuring a reference signal received quality (RSRQ) for each of said beams;
selecting a subset of the measured beams having the highest measured quality; and
reporting the measured quality of each beam in the selected subset of beams to the serving access node.

a signal-to-noise ratio for each of said beams;
a Received Signal Strength Indicator (RSSI) for each of said beams;
a Reference Signal Received Power (RSRP) for each of said beams.

a receiver;
a transmitter; and
a processing circuit operatively coupled to the receiver and transmitter and configured to:

receive from an access node serving the wireless device, with a control channel message, a set of beams to measure comprising an identification of each beam to measure and determined time periods to perform the measurement;
measure a reference signal received quality (RSRQ) for each of said beams;
select a subset of the measured beams having the highest measured quality; and
report the measured quality of each beam in the selected subset of beams to the serving access node.

a signal-to-noise ratio for each of said beams;
a Received Signal Strength Indicator (RSSI) for each of said beams;
a Reference Signal Received Power (RSRP) for each of said beams.

receive from an access node serving the wireless device, with a control channel message, a set of beams to measure comprising an identification of each beam to measure and determined time periods to perform the measurement;
measure a reference signal received quality (RSRQ) for each of said beams;
select a subset of the measured beams having the highest measured quality; and
